  "definition_ja": "a ≠ 0 のとき a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ と定めた、負の整数の指数。",
  "definition_en": "An exponent that is a negative integer, defined by a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ for a ≠ 0.",
  "latex": "a^{-n} = \\frac{1}{a^n}",
  "spoken_en": "a to the negative n equals one over a to the n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": "A negative exponent just means one over — it doesn't make the number negative.",
      "ja": "負の指数は「分の 1」という意味。数が負になるわけではない。",
      "register": "spoken"
    },
    {
      "en": "Write (2x⁻³y²)⁻² without negative exponents.",
      "ja": "(2x⁻³y²)⁻² を負の指数を使わずに表せ。",
      "register": "written"
    }
  ],
  "collocations": [],
  "pitfalls": [
    "x⁻² を −x² とする誤りに注意（The negative exponent does not make it negative.）。用例コーパスの話し言葉では Professor Leonard が最も多く、次が The Organic Chemistry Tutor。",
